# CallGrabbr brand (voice, colors, logo)

Full guide: `docs/BRAND_VOICE.md` · Tokens: `lib/brand.ts`

## Brand reference image (mandatory)

Before creating or editing **any** marketing visual (social graphic, ad, carousel, email header, Canva template):

1. Open **`public/brand_ref.png`** (`nml-main/public/brand_ref.png`).
2. Match its **navy background**, **electric-blue accent**, **cyan→blue→violet hero gradient**, and **logo placement**.
3. Do not invent new palettes or logo treatments. If `brand_ref.png` and `lib/brand.ts` disagree, **`brand_ref.png` wins** — then update `lib/brand.ts`.

## Logo — strict rules

| Asset | Path | Use |
|-------|------|-----|
| Brand board | `public/brand_ref.png` | Reference only — not for publication |
| Full wordmark (HD) | `public/logo_HD.png` | Ads, print, large hero |
| Full wordmark | `public/logo.png` | Web, email |
| Icon | `public/icon.png` / `public/logo_icon.png` | Favicon, avatars, small marks |

**Do:** Use official PNGs only; dark navy backgrounds; clear space ≥ height of the "C" in the wordmark; HD logo above ~200px wide.

**Do not:** Recolor, outline, or gradient-fill the logo; stretch or crop; place on busy photos without a dark scrim; use "Call Grabbr" or "CallGrabber".

